# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the workspace
# Everything in this block is PER-MACHINE. Each computer keeps its own index
# starting at 001, so none of it is shared and a pull can never conflict.
# The corollary: git is NOT a backup of your extracted data -- mirror this
# folder to Drive. See SETUP.md, "Working on more than one computer".

# this machine's index; seed it with tools/init_workspace.py.
# Leading slash matters: without it this would also swallow the template that
# seeds it, docs/templates/paper_source.md, and a clone could not start.
/paper_source.md

# every paper folder -- build script, raw/ inputs and clean_<ID> outputs
[0-9][0-9][0-9]_*/

# every journal sweep folder, and the probe's control runs
journals/J[0-9][0-9]_*/
journals/_control/

# the audit's report and its blind figure reads
AUDIT.md
AUDIT_partial.md
audit/

# ------------------------------------------------- generated skill adapters
# SKILL.md is the Agent Skills open standard, but every tool hard-codes the folder
# it looks in and none can be redirected. So the adapters are GENERATED, never
# committed -- procedures/*.md is the one source of truth, and the repo stays free
# of any vendor's directory. Create them with tools/init_workspace.py.
.agents/
.claude/
.cursor/
.codex/

# ------------------------------------------------------------ caches and scratch
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
~$*.xlsx
.DS_Store
